  "transcript": "Three riddles, three clues each.  Ten seconds to solve each one.  Get all three, and your brain is officially warmed up.  Riddle one, clue one, I repeat everything you say,  but I have no mouth of my own.  Clue two, you can hear me, but you can never see me.  Clue three, the louder you shout, the louder I answer.  Ten seconds go.  In echo, sound bouncing back to you.  Riddle two, clue one, I follow you everywhere in daylight.  Clue two, I copy your every move, but I never make a sound.  Clue three, you can never touch me, but I am always right behind you.  Ten seconds go.  Your shadow, it follows you, but it never makes a sound.  Riddle three, clue one, the more I dry you, the better I become.  Clue two, I hang on a hook and wait for your shower.  Clue three, I soak it all up, then I need to dry out myself.  Ten seconds go.  A towel, the more it dries you, the better it gets.  How many did you solve?  Tell me your score in the comments and send this to a friend who thinks they are clever.",
